 "text": "Teflon was discovered inside a tank that seemed empty. April 6th, 1938, New Jersey. DuPont chemist Roy Plunkett is working on a new gas for refrigerators. He opens a tank of it. Nothing comes out. But the tank still weighs as much as a full one, so they cut it open. Inside, a slippery white waxy powder. The gas had turned into a brand new plastic. By 1941, it has a name. Teflon. Every legend has a beginning.",
